# Seloma AI adapter (Cursor)

Canonical AI engineering knowledge lives in **`.ai/`**, not in duplicated Cursor rules.

Before non-trivial work:

1. Read `.ai/README.md`
2. Read `.ai/rules/core.md` and `.ai/rules/dont-do.md`
3. Classify the task; load only relevant `.ai/rules/*` and `.ai/discovery/*`
4. Follow `.ai/workflows/*` for `/agent-task`, `/agent-review`, `/agent-refactor`, `/agent-debug`
5. Report with `.ai/templates/*`

Do not rebuild Seloma. Do not invent APIs. Prefer existing `packages/api-client`, Nest modules, and Workspace components.

Product docs under `docs/` remain authoritative for product intent; **running code** wins for implementation details.
